{"253517":{"pv":["NS"],"km":948,"cr":"1936","iucn":"II","site":"https://www.pc.gc.ca/en/pn-np/ns/cbreton","wp":"en:Cape_Breton_Highlands_National_Park","f":[["Chéticamp River Cabot Trail Entrance.jpg","Mykola Swarnyk","CC BY-SA 4.0"],["Chéticamp River from the bridge.jpg","Mykola Swarnyk","CC BY-SA 4.0"],["Autumn on the Cabot Trail.jpg","Eric Van Lochem","CC BY-SA 4.0"]],"t":{"pt":{"r":"No norte da ilha de Cape Breton, na Nova Escócia: montanhas, vales, cachoeiras, costões rochosos e um planalto com ar de tundra. Tem o ponto mais alto da província, White Hill, com 533 m.","h":"Criado em 1936, foi o primeiro parque nacional das províncias atlânticas do Canadá. Desde 2014 a Parks Canada trabalha com o instituto mi'kmaq Unama'ki na restauração da floresta boreal.","ff":"Florestas acadiana e boreal. Entre os mamíferos estão alces, linces, ursos-negros, castores e lontras; entre as aves, águias-de-cabeça-branca, gansos-patola e o raro tordo-de-bicknell. É uma Área Importante para Aves.","at":["Cabot Trail, estrada panorâmica que cruza o parque","26 trilhas marcadas, entre elas a Skyline Trail","Vila acadiana de Chéticamp, na entrada oeste","Rios Chéticamp e North Aspy"]},"en":{"r":"On northern Cape Breton Island, Nova Scotia: mountains, valleys, waterfalls, rocky shores and a tundra-like plateau. It holds the province's highest point, White Hill, at 533 m.","h":"Established in 1936, it was the first national park in Canada's Atlantic provinces. Since 2014 Parks Canada has worked with the Mi'kmaw Unama'ki Institute to restore its boreal forest.","ff":"Acadian and boreal forests. Mammals include moose, lynx, black bears, beavers and otters; birds include bald eagles, northern gannets and the rare Bicknell's thrush. It is an Important Bird Area.","at":["The Cabot Trail, a scenic road through the park","26 marked hiking trails, including the Skyline Trail","The Acadian village of Chéticamp at the west entrance","The Chéticamp and North Aspy rivers"]},"es":{"r":"En el norte de la isla de Cape Breton, Nueva Escocia: montañas, valles, cascadas, costas rocosas y una meseta con aspecto de tundra. Tiene el punto más alto de la provincia, White Hill, de 533 m.","h":"Creado en 1936, fue el primer parque nacional de las provincias atlánticas de Canadá. Desde 2014 Parks Canada trabaja con el instituto mi'kmaq Unama'ki en la restauración del bosque boreal.","ff":"Bosques acadiano y boreal. Entre los mamíferos hay alces, linces, osos negros, castores y nutrias; entre las aves, águilas calvas, alcatraces atlánticos y el raro zorzal de Bicknell. Es un Área Importante para las Aves.","at":["La Cabot Trail, carretera panorámica que cruza el parque","26 senderos señalizados, entre ellos el Skyline Trail","El pueblo acadiano de Chéticamp, en la entrada oeste","Los ríos Chéticamp y North Aspy"]}}},"742353":{"pv":["NS"],"km":2363,"cr":"2004-05-01","site":"https://www.dfo-mpo.gc.ca/oceans/mpa-zpm/gully/index-eng.html","wp":"en:Gully_Marine_Protected_Area"},"795176":{"pv":["NS"],"km":404,"cr":"1974-01-01","iucn":"II","site":"http://www.pc.gc.ca/fra/pn-np/ns/kejimkujik/index.aspx","wp":"en:Kejimkujik_National_Park","f":[["Kejimkujik Lake from Kedge Beach - Kejimkujik National Park.jpg","Z3lvs","CC0"],["Harbour Rocks Trail, Kejimkujik Seaside, Nova Scotia (23370548583).jpg","Tony Webster from Portland, Oregon","CC BY-SA 2.0"],["Little River in Fall.jpg","Original uploader was Canoehead at en.wikipedia","Domínio público"],["Kejimkujik Water Colour.jpg","paulhami","CC BY-SA 2.0"],["Still Brook in Fall.jpg","Canoehead at English Wikipedia","Domínio público"]],"t":{"pt":{"r":"No sudoeste da Nova Escócia, com duas partes: uma grande área no interior, cheia de lagos, e o Kejimkujik Seaside, no litoral atlântico. É o único lugar do Canadá que é inteiro parque nacional e sítio histórico nacional.","h":"O nome vem do mi'kmaq, e a Parks Canada o traduz como \"pequenas fadas\". Os mi'kmaq viajam de canoa por esses rios há milhares de anos e deixaram petroglifos. Em 1604 Samuel de Champlain mapeou a costa de Port Mouton.","ff":"Grandes manchas de floresta acadiana, inclusive trechos de floresta antiga. Cerca de 34 espécies de mamíferos, como castores, lontras, ursos-negros e veados; o alce hoje é raríssimo.","at":["Canoagem pelos lagos e rios","Petroglifos mi'kmaq","Céu escuro certificado para observação de estrelas","Praia de St. Catherine's River, no Seaside"]},"en":{"r":"In southwest Nova Scotia, in two parts: a large inland area full of lakes, and Kejimkujik Seaside on the Atlantic coast. It is the only place in Canada that is entirely both a national park and a national historic site.","h":"The name is Mi'kmaq; Parks Canada translates it as \"little fairies\". The Mi'kmaq have canoed these waterways for thousands of years and left petroglyphs. In 1604 Samuel de Champlain mapped the coast at Port Mouton.","ff":"Large tracts of Acadian forest, including some old growth. About 34 mammal species, such as beavers, otters, black bears and deer; moose are now very rare.","at":["Canoeing the lakes and rivers","Mi'kmaw petroglyphs","A certified dark-sky preserve for stargazing","St. Catherine's River Beach at the Seaside"]},"es":{"r":"En el suroeste de Nueva Escocia, en dos partes: una gran zona interior llena de lagos y el Kejimkujik Seaside, en la costa atlántica. Es el único lugar de Canadá que es por completo parque nacional y sitio histórico nacional.","h":"El nombre es mi'kmaq; Parks Canada lo traduce como \"pequeñas hadas\". Los mi'kmaq recorren estos ríos en canoa desde hace miles de años y dejaron petroglifos. En 1604 Samuel de Champlain cartografió la costa de Port Mouton.","ff":"Grandes extensiones de bosque acadiano, incluidos tramos de bosque antiguo. Unas 34 especies de mamíferos, como castores, nutrias, osos negros y ciervos; el alce hoy es rarísimo.","at":["Canoa por lagos y ríos","Petroglifos mi'kmaq","Reserva de cielo oscuro para ver estrellas","La playa de St. Catherine's River, en el Seaside"]}}},"2803410":{"pv":["NS"],"km":7.8,"cr":"1997-06-24","site":"https://parks.novascotia.ca/content/thomas-raddall-provincial-park","f":[["Thomas Raddall Provincial Park august 2017 01.jpg","Fralambert","CC BY-SA 4.0"]]},"2828322":{"pv":["NS"],"iucn":"Ib","wp":"en:Tobeatic_Wilderness_Area","f":[["Aerial of Tobeatic Lake, Tobeatic Wilderness Area, Nova Scotia, June 2026.jpg","NSEasternShoreChemist","CC BY-SA 4.0"]]},"3364659":{"pv":["NS"],"km":0.1,"cr":"1974-12-19","site":"https://parks.novascotia.ca/content/cabots-landing","wp":"en:Cabots_Landing_Provincial_Park","f":[["Cabot Landing Provincial Park.JPG","Skeezix1000","CC BY-SA 3.0"],["Cabot’s landing provincial park.jpg","James Nicholson","CC BY-SA 4.0"],["Cabots Landing Provincial Park (7618626116).jpg","Andrea Schaffer from Sydney, Australia","CC BY 2.0"],["Cabot's Landing (20638281231).jpg","Paul from Hacketts Cove, Canada","CC BY 2.0"],["View from Cabot Landing Provincial Park.JPG","Skeezix1000","CC BY-SA 3.0"]]},"3364672":{"pv":["NS"],"km":0.1,"cr":"1982-08-10","wp":"en:Smuggler's_Cove_Provincial_Park","f":[["SmugglersCoveParkNS.jpg","Wendy Schotsmans","CC BY 2.0"],["SmugglersCoveNS SKS.jpg","ThemindofSarah","CC BY-SA 4.0"],["Parc provincial Le Fourneau 03.jpg","Fralambert","CC BY-SA 4.0"]]},"3364710":{"pv":["NS"],"km":7.2,"cr":"1983-03-29","iucn":"II","site":"http://parks.novascotia.ca/content/cape-smokey","f":[["Kanada 2017 (41963389935).jpg","simpf","CC BY-SA 2.0"],["Yankee Line (19665127775).jpg","KK70088","CC BY-SA 2.0"]]},"4133141":{"pv":["NS"],"km":30,"cr":"2013-12-01","iucn":"II","site":"http://www.pc.gc.ca/eng/pn-np/ns/sable/index.aspx","wp":"en:Sable_Island_National_Park_Reserve","f":[["Stallion and harem on Sable Island.jpg","Paul Gierszewski","CC BY-SA 4.0"],["Lone horse 01.jpg","Paul Gierszewski","CC BY-SA 4.0"]],"t":{"pt":{"r":"Uma ilha de areia em forma de meia-lua no Atlântico Norte, 300 km a sudeste de Halifax, na Nova Escócia. Ficou famosa pelos cavalos selvagens e pelos naufrágios.","h":"O navegador português João Álvares Fagundes passou por ali em 1520-1521 e provavelmente a chamou de \"Fagunda\". Os bancos de areia em volta causaram tantos naufrágios que ela ganhou o apelido de \"cemitério do Atlântico\". Virou reserva de parque nacional em 2013, e toda visita precisa de autorização da Parks Canada.","ff":"Os cavalos de Sable vivem soltos na ilha há mais de dois séculos. A maior colônia de reprodução de focas-cinzentas do mundo e colônias de aves; é Área Importante para Aves.","at":["Cavalos selvagens de Sable","Dunas e praias sem fim","Visita só com autorização, de avião ou navio"]},"en":{"r":"A crescent-shaped sand island in the North Atlantic, 300 km southeast of Halifax, Nova Scotia, famous for its wild horses and shipwrecks.","h":"Portuguese navigator João Álvares Fagundes passed by in 1520-1521 and probably named it \"Fagunda\". Its shifting sandbars caused so many wrecks that it became known as the \"graveyard of the Atlantic\". It became a national park reserve in 2013, and every visit needs Parks Canada's permission.","ff":"Sable Island horses have roamed free here for more than two centuries. The world's largest breeding colony of grey seals and seabird colonies; it is an Important Bird Area.","at":["The wild horses of Sable","Endless dunes and beaches","Visits by permit only, by plane or ship"]},"es":{"r":"Una isla de arena en forma de media luna en el Atlántico Norte, 300 km al sureste de Halifax, Nueva Escocia, famosa por sus caballos salvajes y sus naufragios.","h":"El navegante portugués João Álvares Fagundes pasó por allí en 1520-1521 y probablemente la llamó \"Fagunda\". Sus bancos de arena causaron tantos naufragios que se ganó el apodo de \"cementerio del Atlántico\". Pasó a ser reserva de parque nacional en 2013, y toda visita necesita autorización de Parks Canada.","ff":"Los caballos de Sable viven sueltos en la isla desde hace más de dos siglos. La mayor colonia de cría de focas grises del mundo y colonias de aves; es Área Importante para las Aves.","at":["Los caballos salvajes de Sable","Dunas y playas sin fin","Visitas solo con permiso, en avión o barco"]}}},"4885607":{"pv":["NS"],"km":0.9,"cr":"1975-02-11","site":"https://parks.novascotia.ca/content/ben-eoin","wp":"en:Ben_Eoin_Provincial_Park","f":[["Ben Eoin Provincial Park & Trail.JPG","Ken Heaton","CC BY-SA 4.0"]]},"4927419":{"pv":["NS"],"km":14.1,"cr":"1974-12-19","iucn":"III","wp":"en:Blomidon_Provincial_Park","f":[["Cape Blomidon - Annapolis Valley - NS..JPG","Figure8","CC BY-SA 3.0"],["Blomidon Provincial Park - Minas Basin at low tide.jpg","Tdc","CC BY-SA 4.0"],["Kanada 2017 (41963368555).jpg","simpf","CC BY-SA 2.0"],["Sky, sea, sand (13455639733).jpg","Paul from Hacketts Cove, Canada","CC BY 2.0"],["Cape Blomidon-mid-day.jpg","Peter Sircom Bromley","CC BY-SA 4.0"]]},"5034650":{"pv":["NS"],"km":0.1,"cr":"1998-06-23","iucn":"II","site":"https://parks.novascotia.ca/content/cape-chignecto","wp":"en:Cape_Chignecto_Provincial_Park","f":[["Chignecto acantilado.JPG","Maamarcos","CC BY-SA 4.0"],["Cape D'Or rd near Parrsboro, Nova Scotia.jpg","LeonardoDog","CC BY-SA 4.0"],["Bay of Fundy (7617887422).jpg","Andrea Schaffer from Sydney, Australia","CC BY 2.0"],["Eatonville2.JPG","Bardencj","Domínio público"],["ThreeSistersNS.JPG","Bardencj","Domínio público"]]},"5210770":{"pv":["NS"],"km":0.5,"cr":"1977-01-25","site":"https://parks.novascotia.ca/content/dalem-lake","wp":"en:Dalem_Lake_Provincial_Park"},"5289220":{"pv":["NS"],"km":11.7,"cr":"1981-03-10","site":"https://parks.novascotia.ca/content/dollar-lake","wp":"en:Dollar_Lake_Provincial_Park","f":[["Dollar Lake Provincial Park.jpg","Releafgarden","CC BY-SA 3.0"]]},"6672831":{"pv":["NS"],"km":17.2,"cr":"1984-10-09","wp":"en:Long_Lake_Provincial_Park_(Nova_Scotia)","f":[["Long Lake, Halifax, NS.JPG","See More","CC BY-SA 3.0"],["Halifax NS-00351 - Lake View Trails (26723701613).jpg","Dennis G. Jarvis","CC BY-SA 2.0"],["Halifax NS-00362 - Below the Bridge (27297060146).jpg","Dennis G. Jarvis","CC BY-SA 2.0"],["Summe